 "_comment": "Synonym groups. A query term that appears in a group expands to every term in that group; a term can sit in several groups. How terms match (implemented in scripts/ua.py search, tested in scripts/tests/test_search.py): ASCII terms match whole words, case-insensitive, with hyphens and punctuation as word breaks and a regular English plural (plan->plans, bus->buses, gallery->galleries); a longer word with the same start does not match (plan does not hit plane, tab does not hit table). This applies both to the words the user typed and to the alias terms. Chinese terms match as substrings. A Chinese token that is not an alias term is split greedily into the longest alias terms it contains, and leftover runs of two or more characters are kept when the catalogue contains them and they are not filler words (侧边栏可折叠 -> 侧边栏 + 折叠). Adjacent words that form a group term are read together (dark mode -> dark-mode). Multi-word terms here (tool call) therefore work both as typed phrases and as expansions.",
